The generalization of this construction from a product of
transpositions to a product of general cycles is straightforward.  For
a $m$-cycle $(k_1\, k_2 \ldots k_m)$, the corresponding shuttle is
realized as $m$ directed edges indicating transitions from horizontal
line $k_j$ to horizontal line $k_{j+1}$.  In the directed graph
visualization, the cycle corresponds to a vertex of total degree $2m$,
with outgoing edge marked $k_1$ followed by the incoming edge $k_1$,
then by outgoing edge $k_2$ and so on.  We illustrate this in
Fig.~\ref{fig:diagram}(b) using the cycle $(1\, 2\, 4)$ as an example.


