    64	Exact count of inequivalent minimal cycle factorizations
    65	
    66	Work in the symmetric group on the labels 1,...,11.
    67	Let C be the cycle (1 2 ... 11).  Permutations are composed
    68	right-to-left: in sigma_m ... sigma_1, sigma_1 acts first.
    69	
    70	A cycle factorization of C is a product sigma_m ... sigma_1 = C.
    71	Its type records how many factors have each cycle length.  It is
    72	minimal when sum over its factors of (cycle_length - 1) equals
    73	11 - 1.  Two minimal factorizations are equivalent when one
    74	can be obtained from the other by repeatedly swapping adjacent
