codex
Built a verified Track B generator based on the paper’s rooted-plane-tree bijection and Łukasiewicz-word count. The suggested factor-ordering family was avoided because Theorems 1 and 4 make it constructively easy. [Full paper](https://arxiv.org/html/0809.3476v2).

Deliverables:

- [gen_0809_3476.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0809.3476/gen_0809_3476.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0809.3476/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0809.3476/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0809.3476/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0809.3476/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0809.3476/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Key results:

- Shipping preset: `easy`, `n=24`, seven distinct cycle types.
- All gated self-tests pass.
- Guess resistance: 0/200,000.
- Five attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- Bare oracle loop: hardened, 0/3 solved.
- Structural hint: 0/3 solved.
- Reference DP: 361,472 exact additions across eight instances.
- Compact route: 21 operations; answer is 37 characters and six atoms.
- Fresh audit verified 160 generated instances plus 50 diversity instances.

One non-gating diagnostic remains incomplete: the placebo arm obtained 0/1 scored result, then four HTTP 403 responses because the OpenRouter key reached its total quota. Those errors are preserved and not counted as failures; two further placebo attempts require replenished quota.
